{"id":"finetuning/lora","number":14,"title":"LoRA 低秩更新与冻结基座前向","title_en":"LoRA Low-rank Updates and Frozen-base Forward","paper_id":"lora","paper":{"title":"LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models","authors":"Edward J. Hu et al.","venue":"ICLR 2022","arxiv":"2106.09685v2","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2","anchors":["Section 4.1, Eq. (3): W0 + BA and alpha/r scaling","Section 4.1: random A, zero B initialization and merged inference"]},"type":"implement","parent":null,"difficulty":"E","functions":[{"name":"lora_delta","signature":"lora_delta(a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0) -> Tensor"},{"name":"lora_linear","signature":"lora_linear(x: Tensor, weight: Tensor, a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0, bias: Tensor | None=None) -> Tensor"}],"conventions":{"scope":"Two functions for a linear layer; initialization and a rank-two regression training loop are provided.","determinism":"CPU, seed 42, two Torch threads; no downloads"},"tests":{"T0":1,"T1":1,"T2":3,"T3":1},"t3_budget_s":10,"mutants":[{"id":"m1_missing_rank_scale","bug":"Forget division by rank."},{"id":"m2_train_base","bug":"Accidentally train the base weight."},{"id":"m3_detach_adapter","bug":"Detach the low-rank update."},{"id":"m4_detach_base_input","bug":"Remove the base path gradient to input."}],"viz":["toy_experiment"],"estimated_minutes":25,"formula":"y=xW_0^\\top+\\frac\\alpha r xA^\\top B^\\top","tags":["Post-training","Parameter-efficient Fine-tuning"],"sources_verified":"2026-10-13","module":{"goal":"实现缩放低秩更新并冻结基座参数。","goal_en":"Implement a scaled low-rank update while freezing base parameters.","scope":"实现线性层的两个函数；初始化与 rank-2 回归训练循环已提供。","scope_en":"Two functions for a linear layer; initialization and a rank-two regression training loop are provided.","required_functions":["lora_delta","lora_linear"],"provided_functions":[],"optional":false},"toy":{"provenance":"teaching_adaptation","source":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2","adaptation":"PaperLeet rank-two synthetic regression, not a language-model benchmark.","adaptation_zh":"PaperLeet rank-2 合成回归，不是语言模型基准。","seed":42,"device":"cpu"},"calibration":{"seed":42,"threads":2,"dtype":"float32","method":"Three deterministic reference runs on CPU; independent T2 identities and gradients plus four rejected mutants. Thresholds are explicit exercise requirements, not reproduced paper benchmark scores.","reference_metrics":{"final_mse":2.8140441088453372e-08,"merge_error":3.5762786865234375e-07,"adapter_parameters":28,"base_parameters":48},"max_observed_t3_s":0.04129345889668912},"browser":{"backend":"numpy-autograd-wasm"},"readme":"# LoRA 低秩更新与冻结基座前向\n\n实现缩放低秩更新并冻结基座参数。\n\n论文：[LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models](https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2)。定位：Section 4.1, Eq. (3): W0 + BA and alpha/r scaling；Section 4.1: random A, zero B initialization and merged inference。\n\n## 精选核心\n\n### 返回值要求\n\n#### `lora_delta` — 需要实现\n\n从 a `[r,in_features]`、b `[out_features,r]` 返回一个浮点 Tensor `[out_features,in_features]`，表示经缩放的低秩权重增量。保持共同 dtype/device 及两个 adapter 的梯度。仅返回增量矩阵，不合并进或修改基座权重。\n\n#### `lora_linear` — 需要实现\n\n对 x `[...,in_features]` 返回一个浮点 Tensor `[...,out_features]`，保留所有前导批/token 维度。其值包含基座线性输出和 adapter 贡献，可选 bias 仅加入一次。保持 x 的 dtype/device 及 x、a、b 的梯度；weight 和可选 bias 即使需要梯度也应冻结。不修改输入，也不返回更新后的参数。\n\n### 公式与约定\n\n实现线性层的两个函数；初始化与 rank-2 回归训练循环已提供。\n\n$$\ny=xW_0^\\top+\\frac\\alpha r xA^\\top B^\\top\n$$\n\n- `lora_delta(a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0) -> Tensor`\n- `lora_linear(x: Tensor, weight: Tensor, a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0, bias: Tensor | None=None) -> Tensor`\n\n## 接口与实验\n\n实现 `lora_delta(A,B,alpha)` 与 `lora_linear(x,W,A,B,alpha,bias)`。形状为 `A[r,in]`、`B[out,r]`、`W[out,in]`、`x[...,in]`。增量为 `(alpha/r) * B @ A`。前向等于冻结基座线性映射加低秩更新。即使输入基座权重与 bias 的 `requires_grad=True`，也不能向它们传播梯度；`x`、`A`、`B` 的梯度必须保留。\n\n训练脚手架随机初始化 A、零初始化 B。因此初始输出不变，B 有学习信号而 A 的首次梯度为零。对整个基座计算使用 `no_grad()` 会错误删除部分 x 梯度。将 delta 加到 W 即可合并，测试比较合并前后结果。本模块不包含 dropout。\n\nToy 冻结一个 6×8 映射，用 28 个 adapter 参数拟合已知 rank-2 变化。平台提供输入、优化器和 300 步 CPU 训练。通过表示恢复这个可控目标，不是复现完整语言模型指标。\n\n## Toy 来源\n\n**PaperLeet 教学改编。** PaperLeet rank-2 合成回归，不是语言模型基准。 判题 harness 调用本次提交的函数，保存由其产生的指标与曲线。Lab 静态预览来自参考实现，Run/Submit 的产物来自你的代码。`experiment.py` 与 `tests/` 已提供实验和判题脚手架。\n\n## 来源与验证\n\n[微软 LoRA 官方实现](https://github.com/microsoft/LoRA/blob/main/loralib/layers.py)。题目实现与合成数据由 PaperLeet 编写；论文链接固定公式依据的版本。\n\nT0 验证接口，T1 对照参考值，T2 检查数学性质与梯度，T3 用你的实现运行 toy。在在线编辑器补全 starter 后 Run 或 Submit，无需部署完整大模型训练系统。\n","starter":"import torch\nfrom torch import Tensor\n\ndef lora_delta(a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0) -> Tensor:\n    \"\"\"A [r,in], B [out,r] -> delta W [out,in], scaled by alpha/r.\n\n    Returns:\n        Return one floating Tensor `[out_features,in_features]`, the scaled low-rank weight\n        update, from a `[r,in_features]` and b `[out_features,r]`. Preserve their shared\n        dtype/device and gradients to both adapters. Return the update matrix only, without\n        merging it into or modifying a base weight.\n    \"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError('Implement lora_delta')\n\ndef lora_linear(x: Tensor, weight: Tensor, a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0, bias: Tensor | None=None) -> Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Frozen base and bias; gradients still flow to x and both adapters.\n\n    Returns:\n        Return one floating Tensor `[...,out_features]` from x `[...,in_features]`,\n        preserving every leading batch/token dimension. It contains the base linear output\n        plus adapter contribution, with optional bias included once. Preserve x's\n        dtype/device and gradients to x, a and b; weight and optional bias are frozen even\n        if they require gradients. Do not mutate any input or return updated parameters.\n    \"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError('Implement lora_linear')\n","solution":"import torch\nfrom torch import Tensor\n\n\ndef lora_delta(a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float = 1.0) -> Tensor:\n    \"\"\"A [r,in], B [out,r] -> delta W [out,in], scaled by alpha/r.\"\"\"\n    if a.ndim != 2 or b.ndim != 2 or a.shape[0] < 1 or a.shape[0] != b.shape[1]:\n        raise ValueError('A and B must be rank-compatible matrices with positive rank')\n    return (b @ a) * (alpha / a.shape[0])\n\n\ndef lora_linear(x: Tensor, weight: Tensor, a: Tensor, b: Tensor,\n                alpha: float = 1.0, bias: Tensor | None = None) -> Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Frozen base and bias; gradients still flow to x and both adapters.\"\"\"\n    base = torch.nn.functional.linear(x, weight.detach(), None if bias is None else bias.detach())\n    return base + torch.nn.functional.linear(x, lora_delta(a, b, alpha))\n","notes":"# 实现说明 — LoRA 低秩更新与冻结基座前向\n\n实现 `lora_delta(A,B,alpha)` 与 `lora_linear(x,W,A,B,alpha,bias)`。形状为 `A[r,in]`、`B[out,r]`、`W[out,in]`、`x[...,in]`。增量为 `(alpha/r) * B @ A`。前向等于冻结基座线性映射加低秩更新。即使输入基座权重与 bias 的 `requires_grad=True`，也不能向它们传播梯度；`x`、`A`、`B` 的梯度必须保留。\n\n训练脚手架随机初始化 A、零初始化 B。因此初始输出不变，B 有学习信号而 A 的首次梯度为零。对整个基座计算使用 `no_grad()` 会错误删除部分 x 梯度。将 delta 加到 W 即可合并，测试比较合并前后结果。本模块不包含 dropout。\n\nToy 冻结一个 6×8 映射，用 28 个 adapter 参数拟合已知 rank-2 变化。平台提供输入、优化器和 300 步 CPU 训练。通过表示恢复这个可控目标，不是复现完整语言模型指标。\n\n## 错误变体\n\n- 遗漏除以 rank 的缩放。\n- 错误地训练基座权重。\n- 误 detach 低秩更新，使 adapter 无法学习。\n- 错误移除基座路径对输入的梯度。\n\n每个 mutant 都是相对于参考实现的小幅故意错误。T2 包含独立公式或梯度期望，接受结果不只依赖参考值相等。T3 使用传入的学员实现产生结果。\n\n依据：[2106.09685v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2)；[微软 LoRA 官方实现](https://github.com/microsoft/LoRA/blob/main/loralib/layers.py)。实验来源：PaperLeet rank-2 合成回归，不是语言模型基准。\n","translations":{"en":{"title":"LoRA Low-rank Updates and Frozen-base Forward","readme":"# LoRA Low-rank Updates and Frozen-base Forward\n\nImplement a scaled low-rank update while freezing base parameters.\n\nPaper: [LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models](https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2). Anchors: Section 4.1, Eq. (3): W0 + BA and alpha/r scaling; Section 4.1: random A, zero B initialization and merged inference.\n\n## Selected core\n\n### Return requirements\n\n#### `lora_delta` — Required\n\nReturn one floating Tensor `[out_features,in_features]`, the scaled low-rank weight update, from a `[r,in_features]` and b `[out_features,r]`. Preserve their shared dtype/device and gradients to both adapters. Return the update matrix only, without merging it into or modifying a base weight.\n\n#### `lora_linear` — Required\n\nReturn one floating Tensor `[...,out_features]` from x `[...,in_features]`, preserving every leading batch/token dimension. It contains the base linear output plus adapter contribution, with optional bias included once. Preserve x's dtype/device and gradients to x, a and b; weight and optional bias are frozen even if they require gradients. Do not mutate any input or return updated parameters.\n\n### Formula and conventions\n\nTwo functions for a linear layer; initialization and a rank-two regression training loop are provided.\n\n$$\ny=xW_0^\\top+\\frac\\alpha r xA^\\top B^\\top\n$$\n\n- `lora_delta(a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0) -> Tensor`\n- `lora_linear(x: Tensor, weight: Tensor, a: Tensor, b: Tensor, alpha: float=1.0, bias: Tensor | None=None) -> Tensor`\n\n## Contract and experiment\n\nImplement `lora_delta(A,B,alpha)` and `lora_linear(x,W,A,B,alpha,bias)`. Shapes are `A[r,in]`, `B[out,r]`, `W[out,in]`, and `x[...,in]`. The delta is `(alpha/r) * B @ A`. The forward operation is the frozen base linear map plus this low-rank update. Base weight and optional bias must not receive gradients, even when their inputs have `requires_grad=True`; gradients to `x`, `A`, and `B` must remain intact.\n\nThe training scaffold initializes A randomly and B to zero. Initially, the adapter changes no outputs: B has a nonzero learning signal while A's first gradient is zero. Freezing the entire base computation with `no_grad()` would incorrectly remove part of the gradient to x. Merge by adding the returned delta to W; the exercise compares merged and unmerged outputs. There is no dropout in this module.\n\nThe toy freezes a 6-by-8 map and fits a known rank-two change using 28 adapter parameters. The platform supplies input data, optimizer and 300 CPU training steps. Passing means recovering this controlled target, not reproducing a full language-model benchmark.\n\n## Toy provenance\n\n**PaperLeet teaching adaptation.** PaperLeet rank-two synthetic regression, not a language-model benchmark. The test harness calls your submitted functions and records the resulting metrics and curves. The Lab's static preview comes from the reference; your Run/Submit artifacts come from your code. The experiment and test scaffolding are supplied in `experiment.py` and `tests/`.\n\n## Sources and verification\n\n[Official Microsoft LoRA implementation](https://github.com/microsoft/LoRA/blob/main/loralib/layers.py). All exercise implementations and synthetic data are written for PaperLeet. The paper link pins the version used for the formulas.\n\nT0 checks contracts, T1 compares with the reference, T2 checks mathematical and gradient properties, and T3 runs the toy through your implementation. Implement the starter functions in the online editor, then Run or Submit. The official large-model training system is not required.\n","notes":"# Implementation notes — LoRA Low-rank Updates and Frozen-base Forward\n\nImplement `lora_delta(A,B,alpha)` and `lora_linear(x,W,A,B,alpha,bias)`. Shapes are `A[r,in]`, `B[out,r]`, `W[out,in]`, and `x[...,in]`. The delta is `(alpha/r) * B @ A`. The forward operation is the frozen base linear map plus this low-rank update. Base weight and optional bias must not receive gradients, even when their inputs have `requires_grad=True`; gradients to `x`, `A`, and `B` must remain intact.\n\nThe training scaffold initializes A randomly and B to zero. Initially, the adapter changes no outputs: B has a nonzero learning signal while A's first gradient is zero. Freezing the entire base computation with `no_grad()` would incorrectly remove part of the gradient to x. Merge by adding the returned delta to W; the exercise compares merged and unmerged outputs. There is no dropout in this module.\n\nThe toy freezes a 6-by-8 map and fits a known rank-two change using 28 adapter parameters. The platform supplies input data, optimizer and 300 CPU training steps. Passing means recovering this controlled target, not reproducing a full language-model benchmark.\n\n## Deliberately wrong variants\n\n- Forget division by rank.\n- Accidentally train the base weight.\n- Detach the low-rank update.\n- Remove the base path gradient to input.\n\nEach mutant differs from the reference in a small, intentional change. T2 includes independent formula or gradient expectations, so equality with the reference is not the only acceptance evidence. T3 produces artifacts from the supplied implementation.\n\nSource: [2106.09685v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2); [Official Microsoft LoRA implementation](https://github.com/microsoft/LoRA/blob/main/loralib/layers.py). Toy provenance: PaperLeet rank-two synthetic regression, not a language-model benchmark.\n"}},"vizData":{"provenance":{"kind":"teaching_adaptation","source":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685v2","adaptation":"PaperLeet rank-two synthetic regression, not a language-model benchmark."},"final_mse":2.28521308542895e-08,"merge_error":2.384185791015625e-07,"training":[{"step":0,"mse":0.20706810057163239},{"step":1,"mse":0.19424700736999512},{"step":2,"mse":0.1597725749015808},{"step":3,"mse":0.11476392298936844},{"step":4,"mse":0.07561057060956955},{"step":5,"mse":0.05340680852532387},{"step":6,"mse":0.05053252726793289},{"step":7,"mse":0.05313355103135109},{"step":8,"mse":0.049860987812280655},{"step":9,"mse":0.04113682731986046},{"step":10,"mse":0.03399672731757164},{"step":11,"mse":0.03291131556034088},{"step":12,"mse":0.03577041998505592},{"step":13,"mse":0.03873034939169884},{"step":14,"mse":0.039286211133003235},{"step":15,"mse":0.036623381078243256},{"step":16,"mse":0.03131600096821785},{"step":17,"mse":0.02484809421002865},{"step":18,"mse":0.018